# Rust build output
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Commit workflow scratch (must stay untracked — see COMMIT.md)
git_message_brief.txt

# Generated artifacts are regenerated locally, never tracked (see COMMIT.md)
/generated

# Logs & OS cruft
*.log
.DS_Store

# Note: Cargo.lock is intentionally NOT ignored — binary/application projects should
# commit it for reproducible builds. If this becomes a library-only workspace, add it.

# mdBook build output (regenerate with `make book`, never tracked)
/docs/book/book
/docs/models/*/book

# Python bytecode from the tracked tools under scripts/ — generated, never tracked
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Primary-source materials cache (scripts/materials.py --fetch). Large third-party documents:
# this repository catalogues their identity, revision, digest and licence in the tracked
# materials/catalog.sexp, and does not redistribute the documents themselves. An empty cache is
# the normal state of a fresh clone, not a fault.
/.materials

# External-channel snapshots (MODEL-METHOD.15): local copies of another repository's feed and
# ledger files, taken so the external root path is not needed again. Not a source of truth —
# the tracked catalogue rows adopted from the feed are. The corpus location may be recorded in
# untracked files here (Policy 12 binds tracked files only).
/.semulith-data

# LinkedSpec application-owned data: cargo home, target dir, cache and scratch for the vendored
# submodule, as its integration guide prescribes (docs/linkedspec-book/src/public-api/
# integration-rust.md, "Keep preparation and build products local"). Repo-local by design, so
# Policy 13 holds: every byte lives on the repository's own volume.
/.app-data
